From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm cuda: TF_GLM_OVN_GLUE_FUSE, _GLUE_ROW, _PDL_EARLY

ai-engine 3423859e7 grafted onto the pin stack, after 0021's MLA knobs. GLUE_FUSE runs
each hc_post with the next site's hc_pre in one kernel (cuda_forward_glue.zig), GLUE_ROW
glues a prompt piece of N rows or more in one kernel, and PDL_EARLY launches the glue's
variants programmatic-dependent. The glue kernels gain the fused/_pdl forms
(glm_glue_bmm.cuh, glm_glue_hc.cuh, glm_glue_moe.cuh, glm_glue_norm.cuh, glm_glue_rows.cuh)
and cuda_glue.Kernels carries them. Default off: each site's own kernel, as today.

Pin adaptations: the pin's `post` takes (rank, rows) so the fused path's x is the rank's
own b.x and the three call sites pass (r, R); the pin's L2PF accessor keeps its name
(prefetch) so the shared path calls it unchanged; the pin's Set keeps its own fields and
gains the fused/_pdl ones; the Mla struct is closed properly with read/wanted restored.
Comment lines single-lined.

Gates on pin+0001..0022: check-native-cuda-host green, test-lane-api-host green,
whole-tree fmt green, lean base-vs-head 0 new, fatbins green.

Folded in by the 2026-11-12 fold (work/fold/MAP.tsv), each hunk where it belongs:
- 0037: the KDA block writes its o_proj into `out` again (the line sits on this patch's l2pfFor)
- 0038: the 16-row router kernel this patch's graft dropped
- 0041: the OVN kernels load without an MLA knob, router() launches ROUTER16's kernel, Forward.set passes .mla, .onepass and .onepass_pipe, the L2 prefetch joins after the stream mean, and Kernels.wanted counts KVB8 (the copy this patch adds is the one the term belongs on)
- 0043: the router16 comment on one line, for the lean gate
- 0067: a fused glue's last layer glues the buffer the residual is in

Re-seated on v1.2.7 (93a2e93ecebff8aa52b88e58c5dd222516e69c5f, from pin 9c9bf542) by the 2026-11-12 re-seat (work/reseat/DECISIONS.md):
- lean_check.py's DIRECT_GETENV/HIDDEN_GETENV: every TF_* setting this patch reads is a row of platform/environment.zig with a line in docs/environment.md, read through cuda.ovn or environment, never getenv. Rows: TF_GLM_OVN_GLUE_FUSE, _GLUE_ROW, _PDL_EARLY (u64).
- c0f8e1c4c put tf_glm_router_tile on the shared tf_router_mma::logits tiles and 88267c063 made the SwiGLU kernels glm_swiglu.cuh macros: the fold's hand-written router tile and swiglu bodies are gone, so their _pdl twins (tf_glm_router_tile_pdl, tf_glm_swiglu_512_pdl, tf_glm_swiglu_64_pdl), Kernels' three fields and the two selections are not carried; PDL_EARLY launches the router tile and the SwiGLU rows as v1.2.7 does. The hc, norm and row-glue _pdl forms (our own bodies) are carried.
- DEFERRED, the router and SwiGLU _pdl forms: they need a PDL parameter on upstream's shared tf_router_mma::logits and TF_GLM_SWIGLU_* macros; worth writing only if PDL_EARLY=1 and =2 measure a gain at 1/2/4/6/8 streams over off (no measurement exists, fold-series.md F14).
- Kernels.load calls Mla.wanted(); the fold's second read()/wanted() pair inside Kernels has no caller, and the KVB8 term the fold put on it (0041) never reached the live one, so KVB8 alone loaded null OVN handles. The dead pair is not carried and Mla.wanted() counts KVB8.
- source: work/fold/0026-glue-fuse.patch

